# Coolify Diagnostics Environment Template

Copy these into a **separate** Coolify Application for the diagnostics customer.
Never reuse hospital `DATABASE_URL`, `JWT_SECRET`, or upload volumes.

```bash
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=3000

# Coolify-managed Postgres for THIS org only
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/helty_diagnostics_customer

# Unique per org — required in production (app will refuse example defaults)
JWT_SECRET=generate-a-long-random-string-unique-to-this-customer

HOSPITAL_NAME=Customer Diagnostics Lab
PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://api.diagnostics-customer.example
CORS_ORIGIN=*

USE_REDIS=false

# Optional integrations (leave empty until needed)
POSTMARK_SERVER_TOKEN=
POSTMARK_FROM=
TERMII_API_KEY=
TERMII_BASE_URL=
TERMII_SENDER_ID=

HELITY_DESKTOP_UPLOAD_PASSWORD=unique-desktop-upload-password

# One-shot seed (used when you exec seed:diagnostics — not on every boot)
SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@customer.example
SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=set-a-strong-password
SEED_ADMIN_STAFF_ID=DIAG-ADMIN-001
SEED_ADMIN_FIRST_NAME=Diagnostics
SEED_ADMIN_LAST_NAME=Admin
```

## Coolify storage

Mount a persistent volume at:

```text
/app/uploads
```

Hospital and diagnostics apps must use **different** volumes.
